---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Privacy" description="How Learning Crumbs handles personal information, including what we collect when you register or contribute.">
  <article class="legal">
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <p class="draft"><strong>Draft.</strong> This notice must be reviewed by a solicitor, and checked against the UK GDPR and the ICO's Age Appropriate Design Code, before the site opens to contributors.</p>

    <h2>Who we are</h2>
    <p>Learning Crumbs is run by [name of operator], [address]. We are the controller of the personal information described here. Contact us through the contact page.</p>

    <h2>What we collect</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Browsing the site:</strong> the hosting provider may keep standard server logs, such as IP address and pages requested. We do not add tracking scripts or advertising cookies.</li>
      <li><strong>Contact form:</strong> your name, email address and message, so that we can reply.</li>
      <li><strong>Contributor accounts (when available):</strong> your name or nickname, email address, date of birth confirmation (over 18), your choice of how to be credited, and the content you submit.</li>
      <li><strong>Room suggestions:</strong> the suggestion itself, and your email address only if you ask to be told when it goes live.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Why we use it</h2>
    <p>To run the site and reply to you; to let you contribute once you have registered and accepted the terms; to publish approved content; and to keep the site safe from abuse. Our basis is contract, legitimate interests, and consent where we ask for it.</p>

    <h2>Who we share it with</h2>
    <p>Our service providers only, under contract: Supabase (database, login and file storage), Render (hosting) and GitHub (where the site's code and content are kept). Your email address will not be published. A name or nickname is shown with approved content only if you choose to be credited.</p>

    <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
    <p>Contact messages are kept for as long as needed to reply and deal with the matter. Contributor details are kept while the account is active and for a short period after you delete it, unless the law requires us to keep something for longer. Approved content may be kept as part of the collection.</p>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>You can ask to see, correct or delete your personal information, to object to or restrict its use, and to receive a copy of it. You can also withdraw consent at any time. To do this, contact us. You may complain to the Information Commissioner's Office (ico.org.uk).</p>

    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>Only adults may register or contribute. The site is designed to be used by children with an adult, and we do not knowingly collect personal information from anyone under 18.</p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>We may update this notice and will show the date of the latest change below.</p>

    <p class="updated">Last updated: [date to be added on publication]</p>
  </article>
</Base>
